      <bpmn:userTask id="W3989_Task5" name="HR conduct people DD: org structure and headcount, key talent and retention…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: HR conduct people DD: org structure and headcount, key talent and retention risk, compensation/benefits and comparability (links to VS-102), payroll/statutory compliance (links to VS-19.2), contingent workforce (links to VS-98), and culture/engagement indicators
Responsible (R): HR / Corp Dev
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per target</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3989_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3989_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3989_Task6" name="Labor-Relations/Legal assess labor and union risk: collective bargaining…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Labor-Relations/Legal assess labor and union risk: collective bargaining agreements, union representation and pending labor cases (links to VS-84/NLRC), DOLE compliance, retrenchment/restructuring exposure, and any Philippine labor-law transfer/absorption considerations for acquired employees
Responsible (R): Labor Relations / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO / VP Legal
Duration: Per target</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3989_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3989_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3989_Task7" name="HR quantify people-cost and integration implications (retention, harmonization…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: HR quantify people-cost and integration implications (retention, harmonization, severance), update the model (links to W3981), and design the retention and Day-1 people plan (links to W3994/W3996)
Responsible (R): HR / Corp Dev
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per target</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3989_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3989_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3989_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3989_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
